// Repeated annotations offer many identical subsequences, but only one variable map.
theory DiffVariantRepeatedActions begin
builtins: symmetric-encryption
rule R: [In(x), In(k)] --[A(x), A(x), A(x), A(x), A(x), A(x), A(x), A(x), A(x), A(x), A(x), A(x), A(x), A(x)]-> [Out(sdec(senc(x,k),k))]
left rule R: [In(x), In(k)] --[A(x), A(x), A(x), A(x), A(x), A(x), A(x), A(x), A(x), A(x), A(x), A(x), A(x), A(x)]-> [Out(sdec(senc(x,k),k))]
 variants rule (modulo AC) R___VARIANT_1: [In(y), In(k)] --[A(y), A(y), A(y), A(y), A(y), A(y), A(y), A(y), A(y), A(y), A(y), A(y), A(y), A(y), A(y), A(y), A(y), A(y), A(y), A(y), A(y), A(y), A(y), A(y), A(y), A(y), A(y), A(y)]-> [Out(y)]
right rule R: [In(x), In(k)] --[A(x), A(x), A(x), A(x), A(x), A(x), A(x), A(x), A(x), A(x), A(x), A(x), A(x), A(x)]-> [Out(sdec(senc(x,k),k))]
end
